      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first train from Cincinnati to Indianapolis passed through Batesville on November 1, 1853, marking the town’s early rail connection.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batesville%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between 1867 and 1892, nine furniture, coffin, and novelty factories operated in Batesville, thanks to abundant hardwood timber.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://batesvilleindiana.us/about-batesville/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Schrader Furniture Factory, built in 1873, was rebuilt in 1875 after a fire, illustrating the town’s industrial resilience.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batesville%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Batesville’s Central Historic District was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2011, safeguarding its historic architecture.",
